# VALUEOUS (.antigravityrules) — Drop into root of Valeous-main

## 1. Project & Stack Identity
- Project: VALUEOUS (`VLS-TBP-2026-001`), three-sided marketplace (Customers, Creators, Businesses, Internal Admins).
- Stack: Next.js 15.5 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript 5.8 (strict), Tailwind CSS 3.4, Drizzle ORM + PostgreSQL 17 (`pgTable`), Redis 7 + BullMQ worker (`src/workers/`), Zod 4.6, Vitest + Testcontainers PG, Playwright.
- NEVER use SQLite (`sqliteTable`, `better-sqlite3`) for new code. All new schema and queries target PostgreSQL 17.
- NEVER rewrite to NestJS; extend the existing Next.js modular monolith in `src/server/`.

## 2. Hard Financial & Booking Invariants (NEVER VIOLATE)
- Money is ALWAYS stored as integer paise (`bigint`), NEVER floating-point numbers.
- Timestamps are ALWAYS UTC (`timestamptz`) in the DB; convert to IST only for UI display and offer expiry checks.
- Availability & Reservations: Enforce `CHECK(reserved + confirmed <= capacity)` at DB level and `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` inside transactions. Temporary holds expire in 300 seconds (5 minutes).
- Booking State Machine: Only allow the 12 closed states (`Draft`, `Held`, `Pending Payment`, `Pending Approval`, `Confirmed`, `Checked In`, `Completed`, `Closed`, `Cancelled`, `Refund Pending`, `Refunded`, `Disputed`). Log every transition to `booking_events`.
- Payments: All payment calls go through `src/server/payments/provider.ts` (`PaymentProvider` interface). Browser redirects NEVER confirm a booking—only HMAC-verified webhooks + provider status checks confirm bookings.
- Double-Entry Ledger: `ledger_transactions` and `ledger_entries` are strictly INSERT-ONLY (`SUM(Debits) == SUM(Credits)`). NEVER write `UPDATE` or `DELETE` queries on ledger tables.
- AI Boundary: Booking, payment, and ledger modules must NEVER import AI code.

## 3. UI/UX & Branding Rules (Arpita)
- Use VALUEOUS Blueprint palette in `tailwind.config.ts`: Primary `#2B68C4`, Creator `#84BE82`, Business `#183056`. Remove all orange PromoBridge branding.
- Use "Creator" everywhere in UI copy (never "Influencer").
- Customer booking/detail screens MUST show price, inclusions, exclusions, provider info, and cancellation policy before checkout.
- Creator content/recommendations MUST require `proof_type` (`Visited`, `Researched`, `Gifted`, `Paid`).
- Every async page needs skeleton loaders, plain-language errors with `correlation_id` (no stack traces), and 44px minimum touch targets (WCAG 2.2 AA).

## 4. Repo, Branching & Verification Rules
- Never commit `.env`, API keys, or secrets.
- Branch naming: `feat/vls-<ticket-id>-<short-slug>` (e.g., `feat/vls-103-pg-migration`).
- Before opening a PR to `main`, run and pass:
  1. `npm run typecheck`
  2. `npm run lint`
  3. `npm test`
  4. `npm run build`
- Subham (Tech Admin) reviews and merges all PRs touching `src/server/db/`, `src/server/payments/`, `booking`, or `ledger`.
